-- ako/mxcli#1514 (upstream mendixlabs/mxcli#1604), the negative side: text
-- under an @expect that does not continue the expression is not skipped. Its
-- text runs on to the next @tag or the end of the comment, so the sentence
-- below is part of the assertion, which then cannot be compiled — an ERROR
-- (MDL-TEST01 in check), never a pass on the first line alone. Skipping
-- untagged lines is exactly how the truncation went unseen.
--
--   mxcli check mdl-examples/bug-tests/test-runner-1514-text-after-expect.fail.test.mdl
--
-- fails with: @expect $r = 'a;b' Checks that the separator survives.: unexpected
-- trailing input ... (this @expect spans 2 lines ... put a description before
-- the first tag). Before the fix it passed, asserting $r = 'a;b'.
mdl 1;
/**
 * @test trailing prose
 * @expect $r = 'a;b'
 * Checks that the separator survives.
 */
$r = call microflow Probe.SUB_Make();
/
